From: RadicalES
Subject: [PATCH] cros_gralloc: drop DRM master after opening a node

The kernel makes the first process to open a DRM primary (card) node its
master. On SoCs whose GPU render node has no minigbm backend (RK3588:
renderD128 is panthor), gralloc falls back to the display card node, and
the allocator service, which starts before the composer, ends up as DRM
master. drm_hwcomposer's drmSetMaster() then fails ("DRM/KMS master
access required") and it creates a headless null display.

gralloc only allocates and maps buffers and never needs master, so give
it up right after opening, as minigbm_helpers.c already does.

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
---
 cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
--- a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
+++ b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
@@ -109,6 +109,9 @@ static struct driver *init_try_node(int idx, char const *str)
 	if (fd < 0)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/* No-op on render nodes; on a card node it lets the composer be master */
+	drmDropMaster(fd);
+
 	drv = drv_create(fd);
 	if (!drv)
 		close(fd);
